# The ingested U.S. Code, the Public Law text and the regression corpus are ALL
# tracked.
#
# They used to be ignored, as large regenerable artifacts. They are tracked now
# because the site is deployed from this repo to GitHub Pages, and the shards are
# the site: ignore them and the deploy is an app that resolves nothing, telling
# strangers to run a Python script. ~63,000 files and 322 MB of U.S. Code, plus
# 34 MB of corpus bills. Both are works of the U.S. Government and not subject to
# copyright (see NOTICE).
#
# Regenerate rather than hand-edit:
#   python tools/ingest_usc.py --titles all   # data/usc/
#   python tools/ingest_usc.py --acts-only    # just data/usc/acts/
#   node tools/ingest_plaw.mjs                # data/plaw/  (106 MB, 25 laws)
#   node tools/corpus.mjs fetch               # corpus/files/

# Dev-only dependency for tools/rendertest.mjs (the app itself has none).
# package.json IS tracked: without one, `npm i -D linkedom` walks up and installs
# into the parent directory's package.json, which on a fresh machine meant the
# user's home folder.
node_modules/
bun.lock
bun.lockb

# Python bytecode. tools/ is imported directly by ad-hoc probe scripts when
# checking how source credits parse, which drops a __pycache__ next to it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Stray screenshots dropped in the working tree
Screenshot*.png
